  "live_records": {
    "q-177648": {
      "dom_id": "step-q177648",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130949/assets/5b882f3fb0e7b44eb2df3a510260574e5c4a4d85842a9c0d65515f1a40894756.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,1),$ and $(0,1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130949/assets/cb530698591dbd71a8058d9faa0c60b636dc654f21e92d65ec8295aeaa67355a.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $\\{0\\}\\times [0,1]:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130949/assets/704f8f6f0666d09bb2b8a25eab0548c3eb808e2c9d394d2ae873de35cb0112d1.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
